{"id":"e03t1","name":"No-Show Rate from Appointment Logs","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","input_dir"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A network of clinics logs every change of every appointment as JSON lines. The logs are stored in <code>input_dir</code>, one folder per day: <code>input_dir/day=YYYY-MM-DD/updates.json</code>. Each line of a file is one JSON object with these fields:</p>\n<ul><li><code>appointment_id</code> - the ID of the appointment (string);</li><li><code>patient_id</code> - the patient (string);</li><li><code>doctor</code> or <code>doctor_id</code> - the doctor (string). Old logs use the field <code>doctor</code>; after a migration, new logs use <code>doctor_id</code> instead. A test can contain only old logs or only new logs;</li><li><code>slot</code> - the time of the appointment, <code>\"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\"</code> (string);</li><li><code>status</code> - <code>\"booked\"</code>, <code>\"completed\"</code>, <code>\"no_show\"</code> or <code>\"cancelled\"</code>;</li><li><code>updated_at</code> - when the change was logged, <code>\"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\"</code> (string).</li></ul>\n<p>Some lines are broken (not valid JSON) and must be ignored. The current state of an appointment is its update with the latest <code>updated_at</code>; two updates of the same appointment never have the same <code>updated_at</code>. An appointment can change doctor or slot between two updates: always use the values of the current state.</p>\n<p>Your task is to compute the no-show rate of each doctor per month of the <code>slot</code>, using the current state of every appointment:</p>\n<ol><li><code>appointments</code> - the number of appointments whose current status is not <code>\"cancelled\"</code>;</li><li><code>no_shows</code> - the number of appointments whose current status is <code>\"no_show\"</code>;</li><li><code>no_show_rate</code> - <code>no_shows / appointments</code>, rounded to 2 decimals.</li></ol>\n<p>Return <code>doctor_id</code>, <code>month</code> (string <code>\"YYYY-MM\"</code>), <code>appointments</code>, <code>no_shows</code> and <code>no_show_rate</code>, only for doctor-months with at least one appointment. Sort by <code>month</code>, then <code>no_show_rate</code> descending, then <code>doctor_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/day=2026-02-27/updates.json</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"appointment_id\": \"A1\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-02 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 10:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A2\", \"patient_id\": \"P2\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-03 10:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 11:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A3\", \"patient_id\": \"P3\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-04 11:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 12:00:00\"}\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/day=2026-03-05/updates.json</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"appointment_id\": \"A1\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-02 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 08:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A9\", \"status\": \n{\"appointment_id\": \"A2\", \"patient_id\": \"P2\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_ben\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-03 10:00:00\", \"status\": \"no_show\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 09:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A3\", \"patient_id\": \"P3\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-04 11:00:00\", \"status\": \"cancelled\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 10:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A4\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_ben\", \"slot\": \"2026-04-01 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 11:00:00\"}\n</pre><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>doctor_id</th><th>month</th><th>appointments</th><th>no_shows</th><th>no_show_rate</th></tr><tr><td>dr_ben</td><td>2026-03</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>dr_lam</td><td>2026-03</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0.0</td></tr><tr><td>dr_ben</td><td>2026-04</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0.0</td></tr></table></div>\n<p><code>A2</code> was moved from <code>dr_lam</code> to <code>dr_ben</code>, and its current status is <code>no_show</code>. <code>A3</code> is cancelled, so <code>dr_lam</code> has one appointment left in March.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, input_dir: str) -> DataFrame:\n    logs = spark.read.json(input_dir)\n    # write your code here\n    return logs\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["JSON","schéma qui change","dernière version","Window","groupBy / agg"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":{"root":"input_dir","files":{"day=2026-02-27/updates.json":"{\"appointment_id\": \"A1\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-02 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 10:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A2\", \"patient_id\": \"P2\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-03 10:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 11:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A3\", \"patient_id\": \"P3\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-04 11:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 12:00:00\"}\n","day=2026-03-05/updates.json":"{\"appointment_id\": \"A1\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-02 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 08:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A9\", \"status\": \n{\"appointment_id\": \"A2\", \"patient_id\": \"P2\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_ben\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-03 10:00:00\", \"status\": \"no_show\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 09:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A3\", \"patient_id\": \"P3\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-04 11:00:00\", \"status\": \"cancelled\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 10:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A4\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_ben\", \"slot\": \"2026-04-01 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 11:00:00\"}\n"}},"visible":[{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"day=2026-02-27/updates.json":"{\"appointment_id\": \"A1\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-02 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 10:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A2\", \"patient_id\": \"P2\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-03 10:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 11:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A3\", \"patient_id\": \"P3\", \"doctor\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-04 11:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27 12:00:00\"}\n","day=2026-03-05/updates.json":"{\"appointment_id\": \"A1\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-02 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 08:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A9\", \"status\": \n{\"appointment_id\": \"A2\", \"patient_id\": \"P2\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_ben\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-03 10:00:00\", \"status\": \"no_show\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 09:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A3\", \"patient_id\": \"P3\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_lam\", \"slot\": \"2026-03-04 11:00:00\", \"status\": \"cancelled\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 10:00:00\"}\n{\"appointment_id\": \"A4\", \"patient_id\": \"P1\", \"doctor_id\": \"dr_ben\", \"slot\": \"2026-04-01 09:00:00\", \"status\": \"booked\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05 11:00:00\"}\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["doctor_id","month","appointments","no_shows","no_show_rate"],"rows":[["dr_ben","2026-03",1,1,1.0],["dr_lam","2026-03",1,0,0.0],["dr_ben","2026-04",1,0,0.0]]}},{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"day=2026-01-